<title>ITALY: Montedison H1 96 cons profit 108 bln lire.</title>
<headline>Montedison H1 96 cons profit 108 bln lire.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			108    vs  1,092</p>
<p>    Parent pretax profit		  89    vs    126</p>
<p>Note - Agro-industrial group Montedison said its half year consolidated net profit in 1995 included a capital gain of 985 billion lire from the Montell deal.  </p>
<p>    Cons net sales		    11,605    vs 12,215</p>
<p>    Cons gross operating margin    1,616    vs  1,929</p>
<p>    Cons net operating profit	  982    vs  1,200</p>
<p>Cons profit pre tax and</p>
<p>	   extraordinary gains	   568    vs    657</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gains		   30    vs  1,006</p>
<p>    Net equity			    10,079  vs  9,920</p>
<p>    Cons net debt			  9,341  (down 497 bln)</p>
<p>    Debt/equity ratio		    0.93   vs  0.96</p>
<p>Parent profit (loss) of</p>
<p>	    ordinary activities	   (120) vs    155</p>
<p>Note - Montedison said in a statement group net debt and net debt/equity ratio comparisons were with December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>For Montedison Spa it noted its pretax profit and said it was offsetting previous losses against taxes.</p>
<p>The group said it had reduced holding system costs 34 percent to 29 billion lire.</p>
</text>
